In `scanner/scanner.go`, the `scanComment` function uses `s.progress(ctx, 1)` to skip the `#` character (line 749):

https://github.com/goccy/go-yaml/blob/d4021ff736c7fea2f9b40de179e80205ce52051c/scanner/scanner.go#L749

`progress()` advances `sourcePos` but does not increment `offset`. As a result, the 1 byte for each `#` is never counted in the offset, causing all subsequent tokens to be shifted by `-1` per preceding comment.

```go
// progress: only advances sourcePos (offset is NOT updated)
func (s *Scanner) progress(ctx *Context, num int) {
    ctx.progress(num)
    s.sourcePos += num
}

// progressColumn: advances both offset and sourcePos
func (s *Scanner) progressColumn(ctx *Context, num int) {
    s.column += num
    s.offset += num
    s.progress(ctx, num)
}
```

