Thanks for all the hard work on this lib, really appreciated!

During some recent work, I came came across a pattern that I thought might be nice to have in the lib's example:

- This code cause an infinite recursion, `yaml.Unmarshal` -> `UnmarshalYAML` -> `yaml.Unmarshal` -> ...
  ```go
  type Member struct {
  	Handle string `yaml:"handle"`
  }

  func (m *Member) UnmarshalYAML(data []byte) error {
	if err := yaml.Unmarshal(data, &m); err != nil {
  		return err
  	}

  	if m.Handle == "" {
  		return ErrMissingHandle
  	}

  	return nil
  }
  ```

- A somewhat elegant solution is to use a type alias:

  ```go
  type Member struct {
  	Handle string `yaml:"handle"`
  }

  func (m *Member) UnmarshalYAML(data []byte) error {
  	type M Member
  	var t M
  	if err := yaml.Unmarshal(data, &t); err != nil {
  		return err
  	}
  	*m = Member(t)

  	if m.Handle == "" {
  		return ErrMissingHandle
  	}

  	return nil
  }
  ```

Given that it's a non-obvious pattern that might still be really useful, I'm wondering if it would have its place in the lib's doc, maybe as an example, next to https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/goccy/go-yaml#BytesUnmarshaler?

